492
00:33:11,963 --> 00:33:13,463
I swear I won't just let it slide.

493
00:33:14,263 --> 00:33:15,333
And what if you don't?

494
00:33:15,963 --> 00:33:18,503
- What? - Will you pick a fight with Calvin?

495
00:33:18,633 --> 00:33:21,043
If I have to, I'll do more than just fight him.

496
00:33:45,733 --> 00:33:47,033
And Hee Ju and I...

497
00:33:47,063 --> 00:33:49,133
We don't have the kind of relationship you think we do.

498
00:33:49,203 --> 00:33:51,773
Not that kind of relationship? Then what is it?

499
00:33:51,973 --> 00:33:52,973
Well...

500
00:33:53,773 --> 00:33:55,903
Someone who provided comfort in moments of struggle?

501
00:34:30,743 --> 00:34:33,443
So, Baek Mi Young left here first.

502
00:34:34,513 --> 00:34:36,383
And Won Ho followed right after her.

503
00:34:38,883 --> 00:34:41,353
But what on earth is this?

504
00:34:44,093 --> 00:34:45,093
Hey.

505
00:34:45,193 --> 00:34:46,593
What are you doing?

506
00:34:48,893 --> 00:34:50,633
Lining up all these drinks.

507
00:34:51,063 --> 00:34:53,563
Mom. Mi Young was here yesterday.

508
00:34:54,063 --> 00:34:55,333
Why was that sly fox here?

509
00:34:55,403 --> 00:34:57,063
She'd brought Won Ho clothes and underwear.

510
00:34:57,933 --> 00:35:00,273
I guess she's still worried since he's her husband.

511
00:35:00,543 --> 00:35:01,543
But...

512
00:35:02,003 --> 00:35:03,703
there was another woman besides Mi Young.

513
00:35:05,173 --> 00:35:06,243
What?

514
00:35:06,373 --> 00:35:07,383
Another woman? Who?

515
00:35:07,443 --> 00:35:08,713
I don't know who she was.

516
00:35:09,383 --> 00:35:10,413
But...

517
00:35:10,753 --> 00:35:12,383
that woman and Won Ho left together.

518
00:35:13,313 --> 00:35:14,583
The three of them left, including Mi Young.

519
00:35:14,923 --> 00:35:17,183
Try to make some sense.

520
00:35:17,323 --> 00:35:18,623
So you're saying the three of them...

521
00:35:18,693 --> 00:35:20,223
were at the motel together yesterday?

522
00:35:20,293 --> 00:35:21,863
Yes, that's what I'm saying.

523
00:35:22,393 --> 00:35:24,463
I don't get it at all either.

524
00:35:26,333 --> 00:35:28,263
So there is another woman?

525
00:35:32,203 --> 00:35:33,633
Oh, dear.

526
00:35:46,483 --> 00:35:47,483
Strange...

527
00:35:53,963 --> 00:35:55,423
"Bae Su Ji?"

528
00:36:13,313 --> 00:36:15,213
You're very talented.

529
00:36:15,583 --> 00:36:16,583
I was very impressed with your work.

530
00:36:17,143 --> 00:36:21,453
Thank you. By the way, is CEO Ji not here?

531
00:36:23,023 --> 00:36:24,553
He's very busy today.

532
00:36:25,053 --> 00:36:26,253
That's why I'm here instead.

533
00:36:27,523 --> 00:36:28,523
I see.

534
00:36:54,183 --> 00:36:55,683
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

535
00:36:58,053 --> 00:36:59,093
(Photographer Ahn Hee Ju)

536
00:37:03,723 --> 00:37:04,733
From this moment on,

537
00:37:04,733 --> 00:37:06,133
don't even think about playing with fire.

538
00:37:06,333 --> 00:37:08,533
Whether you're awake or asleep, watch out for fire.

539
00:37:09,163 --> 00:37:11,903
Right, be careful with fire. Be careful.

540
00:37:19,673 --> 00:37:22,813
Why isn't my hair working today?

541
00:37:25,453 --> 00:37:26,713
Don't tell me you still have feelings for her.

542
00:37:27,353 --> 00:37:28,353
What?

543
00:37:28,453 --> 00:37:30,123
I mean, you're going to see your ex-wife.

544
00:37:30,183 --> 00:37:31,723
Why are you putting in so much effort?

545
00:37:31,823 --> 00:37:33,693
No, Ha Neul said he wanted to see his mom at work,

546
00:37:33,753 --> 00:37:34,763
so I'm taking him.

547
00:37:35,993 --> 00:37:36,993
But you never know, right?

548
00:37:37,493 --> 00:37:40,163
I might run into someone from the film industry.

549
00:37:40,563 --> 00:37:43,763
And then if I get a chance, my screenplay...

550
00:37:44,473 --> 00:37:47,103
Anyway, you know how important first impressions are.

551
00:37:47,643 --> 00:37:49,703
Are you going to Ha Neul's mom's film company now?

552
00:37:50,713 --> 00:37:51,713
Yes.

553
00:37:53,343 --> 00:37:54,513
But Mom, where are you going?

554
00:37:54,643 --> 00:37:56,113
I'm going tiger hunting.

555
00:38:04,723 --> 00:38:07,423
Now that the participants for the senior event are all set,

556
00:38:08,163 --> 00:38:09,623
I guess we can start working.

557
00:38:11,063 --> 00:38:13,293
I'm counting on you. Do a great job.

558
00:38:13,633 --> 00:38:15,903
It's no trouble. I'm getting paid for it, after all.

559
00:38:18,533 --> 00:38:20,773
By the way, from now on, for this kind of work,

560
00:38:21,273 --> 00:38:23,173
I'd appreciate it if you sent a staff member instead.

561
00:38:23,873 --> 00:38:25,643
After all, you're the CEO of a hotel.

562
00:38:26,113 --> 00:38:27,943
Running around for a single document like this,

563
00:38:28,083 --> 00:38:29,083
don't you think that's a bit much?

564
00:38:30,213 --> 00:38:31,553
You're right. I'll do that from now on.

565
00:38:32,983 --> 00:38:35,153
But I came today because I had something...

566
00:38:35,223 --> 00:38:36,423
to give you in person.

567
00:38:45,263 --> 00:38:46,263
Is this...

568
00:38:47,463 --> 00:38:48,463
That's right.

569
00:38:49,433 --> 00:38:52,603
It's the ring your mother gave me before she passed.

570
00:38:54,843 --> 00:38:57,873
It was a precious ring she gave me, asking me to take good care of you.

571
00:38:59,213 --> 00:39:00,413
I missed my chance to return it,

572
00:39:00,473 --> 00:39:02,143
and I've been holding onto it all this time.

573
00:39:04,953 --> 00:39:05,953
But at least for today,

574
00:39:06,783 --> 00:39:08,883
I knew I had to give it back to you.

575
00:39:10,253 --> 00:39:11,253
Today...

576
00:39:12,523 --> 00:39:13,993
It's the anniversary of your parents' death.

577
00:39:21,963 --> 00:39:23,933
You remembered that?

578
00:39:25,303 --> 00:39:26,933
I've never forgotten, not even for a moment.

579
00:39:31,443 --> 00:39:33,673
You have a visitor.

580
00:39:34,213 --> 00:39:35,583
Should I come back later?

581
00:39:35,783 --> 00:39:36,783
Oh, no, that's all right.

582
00:39:37,853 --> 00:39:38,853
Well, I'll be going then.

583
00:39:43,583 --> 00:39:45,693
Oh, fancy seeing you here.

584
00:39:46,953 --> 00:39:47,963
Oh, yes.

585
00:39:49,093 --> 00:39:50,093
Hello.

586
00:39:50,163 --> 00:39:51,593
Yes, hello.

587
00:39:58,533 --> 00:39:59,533
Wait.

588
00:40:00,533 --> 00:40:03,673
- That man just now... - Excuse me, Lawyer, one moment.

589
00:40:11,853 --> 00:40:12,853
Wait a second.

590
00:40:15,783 --> 00:40:16,783
Take this with you.

591
00:40:19,793 --> 00:40:22,793
My mom gave this to you, so you should keep it.

592
00:40:24,233 --> 00:40:25,233
And...

593
00:40:26,063 --> 00:40:28,203
thank you for remembering the anniversary.

594
00:40:28,433 --> 00:40:29,833
(J&White)

595
00:40:37,243 --> 00:40:39,843
Nothing is going on between those two, right?

596
00:40:39,913 --> 00:40:41,543
I'm just overthinking this, right?

597
00:40:42,183 --> 00:40:44,183
You're writing a romance novel over here.

598
00:40:46,953 --> 00:40:48,583
Why are you asking me?

599
00:40:49,183 --> 00:40:50,183
If you're that curious,

600
00:40:50,253 --> 00:40:51,853
there's a fortune-teller at the intersection up ahead.

601
00:40:51,923 --> 00:40:52,923
Go ask them.

602
00:40:55,123 --> 00:40:57,293
How do you expect to get a divorce, acting like this?

603
00:40:58,293 --> 00:41:00,663
My wife used to absolutely hate that jerk.

604
00:41:00,933 --> 00:41:03,163
But today, something felt different.

605
00:41:04,003 --> 00:41:07,373
The vibe between them was definitely different than usual.

606
00:41:08,643 --> 00:41:09,873
If you're that worried about it,

607
00:41:10,643 --> 00:41:13,113
you should write her a love letter, not a legal response.

608
00:41:13,643 --> 00:41:14,943
At least that would be more honest.

609
00:41:19,553 --> 00:41:22,323
- Excuse me a moment. - Go ahead.

610
00:41:24,393 --> 00:41:25,393
What is it?

611
00:41:26,553 --> 00:41:28,693
I'm in a meeting with my lawyer. What's wrong?

612
00:41:30,863 --> 00:41:33,133
Another woman? What are you talking about?

613
00:41:33,493 --> 00:41:34,463
No, it's nothing like that.

614
00:41:34,533 --> 00:41:35,963
Why would Seung Ho say something so ridiculous?

615
00:41:37,063 --> 00:41:39,733
I don't know. I'm busy. I'll call you back.

616
00:41:41,343 --> 00:41:42,343
Jeez.

617
00:41:42,973 --> 00:41:44,543
Who was that, for you to answer the phone like that?

618
00:41:45,073 --> 00:41:46,073
Just a debt collector.

619
00:41:46,713 --> 00:41:49,013
So, where were we?

620
00:41:51,183 --> 00:41:54,623
Excuse me, are you Bae Su Ji, the lawyer?

621
00:41:55,523 --> 00:41:56,823
Yes.

622
00:41:57,183 --> 00:41:59,553
So you're Bae Su Ji? You crazy witch.

623
00:41:59,653 --> 00:42:02,323
Hey, get over here. Who do you think you're seducing, you little tramp?

624
00:42:02,393 --> 00:42:03,923
Why are you hitting on my son?

625
00:42:04,293 --> 00:42:05,293
It's my mom.

626
00:42:05,363 --> 00:42:07,563
What did you say? You little...

627
00:42:08,163 --> 00:42:12,233
- How dare you hit on my son? - Mom, what are you doing?

628
00:42:12,803 --> 00:42:14,703
You crazy fool. You jerk.

629
00:42:14,773 --> 00:42:17,443
Did you really pick your lawyer based on their looks?

630
00:42:18,173 --> 00:42:19,813
Ma'am, please calm down.

631
00:42:19,913 --> 00:42:21,483
Get off me. You pathetic fool, did you run out on...

632
00:42:21,543 --> 00:42:23,243
your family just to fool around with this young thing?

633
00:42:23,343 --> 00:42:24,453
Is that why you ran away from home?

634
00:42:24,613 --> 00:42:25,613
Mom.

635
00:42:25,683 --> 00:42:28,623
You jerk. You absolute jerk.

636
00:42:29,083 --> 00:42:30,993
Stop right there.

637
00:42:31,793 --> 00:42:33,453
That actually hurts.

638
00:42:36,893 --> 00:42:38,693
Ryu Mi Soon.

639
00:42:40,163 --> 00:42:41,703
How have you not changed one bit?

640
00:42:44,133 --> 00:42:45,133
Su Ji?

641
00:42:52,473 --> 00:42:53,473
Let's go.

642
00:42:56,143 --> 00:42:57,313
How can I help you?

643
00:42:57,683 --> 00:43:00,053
Yes, I'm here to see Director Song Woo Young.

644
00:43:00,413 --> 00:43:01,983
We have an appointment to meet at two o'clock.

645
00:43:02,283 --> 00:43:04,153
And you are...

646
00:43:04,493 --> 00:43:07,093
I'm the father of the director's son.

647
00:43:07,523 --> 00:43:08,693
And this is her son.

648
00:43:08,993 --> 00:43:10,723
Ha Neul, what are you doing? Go on and say hello.

649
00:43:10,893 --> 00:43:12,063
Hello.

650
00:43:12,433 --> 00:43:14,333
- Please wait a moment. - Okay.

651
00:43:26,113 --> 00:43:27,113
Yes.

652
00:43:33,513 --> 00:43:36,053
Ha Neul, it looks like your mom's very busy.

653
00:43:36,583 --> 00:43:37,583
Let's come back later.

654
00:43:42,063 --> 00:43:44,193
(Bae Su Ji Law Office)

655
00:43:54,273 --> 00:43:56,403
But Mom, how did you find this place anyway?

656
00:43:56,743 --> 00:43:58,543
Oh, please. How do you think?

657
00:43:59,213 --> 00:44:01,743
I saw the business card in your motel room, of course.

658
00:44:03,583 --> 00:44:05,483
But I had no idea that Bae Su Ji was him.

659
00:44:06,113 --> 00:44:07,413
I never would have dreamed it.

660
00:44:07,683 --> 00:44:09,423
Whether you knew it was me or not,

661
00:44:10,753 --> 00:44:13,023
that was still out of line.

662
00:44:14,323 --> 00:44:17,593
Wait, so are you saying you two are friends from back home?

663
00:44:18,333 --> 00:44:20,693
Yes, Father Kwon and us.

664
00:44:21,463 --> 00:44:24,473
The three of us have been friends since we were kids.

665
00:44:27,033 --> 00:44:29,473
Anyway, Su Ji, it's so good to see you.

666
00:44:30,273 --> 00:44:33,373
I'd heard bits and pieces about you now and then,

667
00:44:33,573 --> 00:44:35,813
but I had no idea you were so close by.

668
00:44:36,283 --> 00:44:38,113
I'll be sure to come by often, Su Ji.

669
00:44:38,353 --> 00:44:40,513
No, you really don't have to do that.

670
00:44:40,653 --> 00:44:42,823
Seeing you this one time is more than enough.

671
00:44:42,983 --> 00:44:47,823
What do you mean, one time? Su Ji, are you eating properly?

672
00:44:48,723 --> 00:44:51,563
You look even paler than you did when you were young.

673
00:44:53,133 --> 00:44:55,163
I'll have to bring you some side dishes.

674
00:45:01,273 --> 00:45:03,803
Mom, let's go. My consultation time is up for today. Let's go.

675
00:45:04,103 --> 00:45:05,913
- Su Ji, do you like braised beef? - Let's go.

676
00:45:06,013 --> 00:45:07,013
What about pickled wild garlic?

677
00:45:07,643 --> 00:45:10,083
I have some delicious seasoned vegetables at home.

678
00:45:10,443 --> 00:45:11,813
I'll be back, Su Ji.

679
00:45:26,133 --> 00:45:27,163
Mom, Dad.

680
00:45:29,163 --> 00:45:30,163
Have you been well?

681
00:45:30,433 --> 00:45:32,573
(The Late Baek Cheol Gyu, The Late Kang Gyeong Hui)

682
00:45:32,633 --> 00:45:34,903
Life got so busy. It's been too long, hasn't it?

683
00:45:36,343 --> 00:45:37,343
I'm sorry.

684
00:45:41,183 --> 00:45:42,543
It's not like I was doing anything that important.

685
00:45:47,183 --> 00:45:48,683
Your only daughter...

686
00:45:50,623 --> 00:45:51,623
has been...

687
00:45:52,823 --> 00:45:54,963
I was so focused on my own struggles that I neglected you.

688
00:45:55,493 --> 00:45:57,463
(The Late Baek Cheol Gyu, The Late Kang Gyeong Hui)

689
00:45:57,523 --> 00:46:00,863
Mom, Dad, you remember Calvin, don't you?

690
00:46:03,963 --> 00:46:04,973
Calvin,

691
00:46:06,133 --> 00:46:08,403
he's the one who told me today was the anniversary of your passing.

692
00:46:13,443 --> 00:46:15,183
The anniversary that even I had forgotten,

693
00:46:16,843 --> 00:46:18,353
Calvin remembered.

694
00:46:18,453 --> 00:46:21,523
(The Late Baek Cheol Gyu, The Late Kang Gyeong Hui)

695
00:46:24,593 --> 00:46:26,723
I should have lived a better life.

696
00:46:30,793 --> 00:46:31,793
I'm sorry.

697
00:46:32,963 --> 00:46:34,163
I'm sorry, Dad.

698
00:46:46,543 --> 00:46:50,313
(The Late Baek Cheol Gyu, The Late Kang Gyeong Hui)

699
00:47:07,563 --> 00:47:10,733
One of my employees made a huge mistake.

700
00:47:11,473 --> 00:47:14,673
While organising the dress list for the senior wedding couples,

701
00:47:15,403 --> 00:47:18,143
they must have mixed up two clients with the same name.

702
00:47:18,643 --> 00:47:21,543
The dress designs and measurements got swapped,

703
00:47:22,983 --> 00:47:25,513
so it looks like we'll have to remake them.

704
00:47:27,913 --> 00:47:29,053
Oh, I see.

705
00:47:30,383 --> 00:47:33,053
Does that mean you have to postpone the wedding?

706
00:47:33,593 --> 00:47:34,893
That would be ideal, but...

707
00:47:35,463 --> 00:47:37,923
the wedding date has already been announced.

708
00:47:38,863 --> 00:47:39,963
Don't worry about that.

709
00:47:40,493 --> 00:47:41,803
I'll take care of it.

710
00:47:42,533 --> 00:47:44,163
I'm sorry to cause you trouble.

711
00:47:44,803 --> 00:47:47,533
Not at all. Mistakes happen at work.

712
00:47:49,943 --> 00:47:52,373
Don't worry too much about it. It's not a big deal.

713
00:47:53,313 --> 00:47:54,613
I can make any adjustments you need.

714
00:47:58,783 --> 00:47:59,783
Pretending you agree when you don't, pretending you like things you hate,

715
00:47:59,853 --> 00:48:00,853
sucking up to people,

716
00:48:00,913 --> 00:48:03,083
and acting like a phony.

717
00:48:03,823 --> 00:48:04,893
What's that if not a clown?

718
00:48:05,823 --> 00:48:07,223
I don't want to stoop to that level.

719
00:48:07,593 --> 00:48:10,523
So, you refuse to change the design no matter what, is that it?

720
00:48:10,723 --> 00:48:12,733
I'm absolutely not changing it.

721
00:48:13,033 --> 00:48:15,433
Not without a request from Man Ju. Not even if the sky falls.

722
00:48:18,073 --> 00:48:20,003
- Mi Young. - Yes?

723
00:48:20,173 --> 00:48:21,543
Since you're here, would you like...

724
00:48:21,603 --> 00:48:23,373
to see the wedding hall construction site?

725
00:48:24,303 --> 00:48:25,313
A wedding hall?

726
00:48:25,743 --> 00:48:28,283
We're building a wedding hall for our own brand.

727
00:48:28,913 --> 00:48:29,913
Calvin Wedding Hall.

728
00:48:30,513 --> 00:48:32,383
The interior isn't even done,

729
00:48:32,753 --> 00:48:34,283
and it's still in the very early stages.

730
00:48:35,553 --> 00:48:37,353
So I was hoping you could take a look...

731
00:48:37,423 --> 00:48:38,993
and give me some good feedback.

732
00:48:40,453 --> 00:48:42,063
Why is my opinion that important?

733
00:48:43,323 --> 00:48:44,393
Because it's your opinion.

734
00:48:46,033 --> 00:48:47,333
If you give me any feedback at all,

735
00:48:47,793 --> 00:48:49,603
it would be a huge help to me.

736
00:48:51,303 --> 00:48:52,303
Would you?

737
00:49:18,133 --> 00:49:19,133
Take a look over there.

738
00:49:21,663 --> 00:49:24,503
- So that's the indoor wedding hall? - That's right.

739
00:49:26,273 --> 00:49:27,973
Where will the seating be arranged?

740
00:49:28,033 --> 00:49:30,103
Wait a minute. Ms. Park.

741
00:49:30,473 --> 00:49:31,473
Ah, yes.

742
00:49:32,943 --> 00:49:34,713
Let's hear what CEO Baek has to say.

743
00:49:35,083 --> 00:49:36,843
Yes.

744
00:49:37,983 --> 00:49:42,853
I want the flowers to connect to the stage.

745
00:49:46,853 --> 00:49:48,663
And if the seating is arranged this way,

746
00:49:48,723 --> 00:49:50,223
is the entrance over there?

747
00:50:00,903 --> 00:50:02,103
Thanks for today, Mi Young.

748
00:50:02,873 --> 00:50:03,873
Don't mention it.

749
00:50:04,073 --> 00:50:06,543
Anyway, I'll have the dresses made as soon as possible...

750
00:50:06,773 --> 00:50:08,643
so there are no delays with the wedding schedule.

751
00:50:09,183 --> 00:50:10,183
Thanks.

752
00:50:13,313 --> 00:50:14,313
You should get going.

753
00:50:14,783 --> 00:50:17,583
Oh, okay. Take care.

754
00:50:30,633 --> 00:50:32,473
Well, isn't this a sight?

755
00:50:34,573 --> 00:50:36,803
Now you're just flaunting your little romance in public.

756
00:50:38,173 --> 00:50:39,173
What?

757
00:50:39,273 --> 00:50:40,273
It's still work hours.

758
00:50:40,343 --> 00:50:41,743
Don't you think you're going too far?

759
00:50:41,813 --> 00:50:43,213
There are other people watching.

760
00:50:43,413 --> 00:50:44,513
People watching?

761
00:50:46,213 --> 00:50:48,223
Do you really have the right to say that to me?

762
00:50:48,553 --> 00:50:49,553
What about me?

763
00:50:49,653 --> 00:50:52,393
Have I ever once slacked off during work hours?

764
00:50:52,653 --> 00:50:56,423
So you did that because it wasn't during work hours?

765
00:50:56,793 --> 00:50:57,793
"That?"

766
00:50:57,923 --> 00:51:00,533
What do you call spending the night in a motel with another woman?

767
00:51:00,793 --> 00:51:02,203
Hey, how many times do I have to tell you...

768
00:51:02,263 --> 00:51:03,263
it was a misunderstanding?

769
00:51:03,403 --> 00:51:07,203
I saw it with my own two eyes, so what is there to misunderstand?

770
00:51:07,403 --> 00:51:10,203
Fine. Then keep thinking that.

771
00:51:13,373 --> 00:51:15,113
And where are you going during work hours?

772
00:51:15,383 --> 00:51:16,483
I'm going to get food.

773
00:51:17,043 --> 00:51:18,883
Because I've been working so hard I haven't even eaten.

774
00:51:23,723 --> 00:51:24,723
Unbelievable.

775
00:51:25,293 --> 00:51:27,423
That's not strong enough.

776
00:51:28,393 --> 00:51:31,463
If there had been some PDA, it might be a different story.

777
00:51:32,933 --> 00:51:35,103
Just the fact that they came out of a motel together...

778
00:51:36,133 --> 00:51:38,203
doesn't carry much weight legally.

779
00:51:40,233 --> 00:51:41,233
I see.

780
00:51:41,573 --> 00:51:43,143
But now that we have a reason to be suspicious,

781
00:51:43,643 --> 00:51:44,673
it's worth keeping a close eye on them,

782
00:51:44,743 --> 00:51:45,743
don't you think?

783
00:51:51,143 --> 00:51:54,113
How do you and Calvin know each other?

784
00:51:54,783 --> 00:51:55,783
What?

785
00:51:56,453 --> 00:51:57,553
A little while ago,

786
00:51:58,453 --> 00:51:59,453
at the office.

787
00:52:00,323 --> 00:52:02,163
Oh, that's...

788
00:52:03,493 --> 00:52:06,563
We're collaborating on a project for work.

789
00:52:06,893 --> 00:52:09,463
So that's what it is.

790
00:52:10,633 --> 00:52:12,433
Then, as for you, a lawyer,

791
00:52:13,373 --> 00:52:15,073
how do you know him?

792
00:52:16,043 --> 00:52:17,243
Calvin...

793
00:52:17,943 --> 00:52:19,513
was my client.

794
00:52:19,943 --> 00:52:23,183
I handled his divorce.

795
00:52:24,143 --> 00:52:25,153
I see.

796
00:52:25,883 --> 00:52:27,013
You and Calvin...

797
00:52:27,553 --> 00:52:28,683
Is something going on between you two?

798
00:52:30,753 --> 00:52:31,753
It's just...

799
00:52:32,523 --> 00:52:33,893
a lawyer's intuition, shall we say.

800
00:52:37,663 --> 00:52:38,733
Before I got married,

801
00:52:39,763 --> 00:52:41,633
we used to date.

802
00:52:42,763 --> 00:52:43,803
Don't tell me...

803
00:52:44,503 --> 00:52:47,303
you were Calvin's first love?

804
00:52:51,043 --> 00:52:52,413
What are the odds of us meeting like this?

805
00:52:55,383 --> 00:52:57,543
That's all in the past now.

806
00:52:57,783 --> 00:53:00,353
To say it's all in the past,

807
00:53:01,653 --> 00:53:03,953
isn't this a little too shocking?

808
00:53:04,883 --> 00:53:05,893
What?

809
00:53:06,153 --> 00:53:07,153
By any chance,

810
00:53:07,853 --> 00:53:10,663
do you know why Calvin got divorced? Or rather,

811
00:53:11,393 --> 00:53:13,063
why he got married...

812
00:53:14,363 --> 00:53:15,333
in the first place?

813
00:53:16,103 --> 00:53:19,003
The woman he was secretly seeing at the time...

814
00:53:19,903 --> 00:53:21,173
got pregnant.

815
00:53:22,103 --> 00:53:23,373
I figured you wouldn't know.

816
00:53:24,543 --> 00:53:25,543
To be honest,

817
00:53:25,743 --> 00:53:29,113
it's a pretty well-known story among those in the know.

818
00:53:31,113 --> 00:53:32,313
Seven years ago,

819
00:53:33,453 --> 00:53:35,123
Calvin and his half-brothers...

820
00:53:36,323 --> 00:53:38,223
apparently had a dispute over control of the company.

821
00:53:38,553 --> 00:53:39,553
Yes.

822
00:53:42,193 --> 00:53:43,823
You've had a tough time, haven't you?

823
00:53:44,263 --> 00:53:45,763
Let's just relax and eat today.

824
00:53:46,193 --> 00:53:47,863
The very day he went to his family's home...

825
00:53:47,933 --> 00:53:49,363
to make up with his half-brothers...

826
00:53:50,203 --> 00:53:51,203
Cheers.

827
00:53:51,263 --> 00:53:53,773
- Cheers. - That's when it all happened.

828
00:53:54,133 --> 00:53:56,173
- This is nice, right? - What do you want to eat? Cake?

829
00:53:56,243 --> 00:53:58,373
- It'll be fine. - You can't get drunk.

830
00:53:58,443 --> 00:54:00,973
- It's fine, it's fine. - Let's have another drink.

831
00:54:14,693 --> 00:54:16,823
I'm... I'm fine.

832
00:54:35,983 --> 00:54:37,243
His half-brothers...

833
00:54:38,243 --> 00:54:41,083
intentionally set a trap for Calvin,

834
00:54:44,023 --> 00:54:45,553
and he fell for it,

835
00:54:45,953 --> 00:54:47,893
ending up marrying that woman.

836
00:54:55,203 --> 00:54:58,773
His brothers said if he just gave up his management rights,

837
00:54:59,233 --> 00:55:01,573
they would cover everything up.

838
00:55:02,473 --> 00:55:05,873
But apparently, he refused.

839
00:55:08,213 --> 00:55:12,583
The entire family was caught up in a soap opera of epic proportions.

840
00:55:14,653 --> 00:55:15,653
And...

841
00:55:16,853 --> 00:55:18,723
the biggest victim in that whole drama...

842
00:55:19,423 --> 00:55:21,023
is sitting right in front of me.

843
00:55:36,273 --> 00:55:37,273
CEO Ji.

844
00:55:37,973 --> 00:55:39,143
Where are you going?

845
00:55:40,843 --> 00:55:41,983
Stop.

846
00:55:46,613 --> 00:55:47,753
What the?

847
00:55:50,853 --> 00:55:53,523
- Stop. - Why are you running away?

848
00:55:54,453 --> 00:55:55,793
Let's do this.

849
00:55:55,893 --> 00:55:58,733
That thing we agreed on, about meeting three times.

850
00:56:00,233 --> 00:56:01,833
Let's just call it off.

851
00:56:02,463 --> 00:56:03,463
What?

852
00:56:03,563 --> 00:56:04,733
I am really sorry,

853
00:56:04,863 --> 00:56:07,233
but I am just not in a position to do that right now.

854
00:56:08,303 --> 00:56:10,173
Then you should have just said so.

855
00:56:10,673 --> 00:56:12,273
Why are you making a fool out of me?

856
00:56:13,443 --> 00:56:14,443
Is it perhaps...

857
00:56:14,913 --> 00:56:16,213
because of your wife?

858
00:56:19,153 --> 00:56:22,523
No, that is just a misunderstanding. Nothing happened between us.

859
00:56:22,923 --> 00:56:25,523
Still, she saw us together at the motel,

860
00:56:26,023 --> 00:56:27,053
so it's understandable she misunderstood.

861
00:56:28,123 --> 00:56:29,963
If that is how you feel,

862
00:56:30,693 --> 00:56:31,893
there is nothing I can do.

863
00:56:37,633 --> 00:56:40,103
Actually, before I go,

864
00:56:40,733 --> 00:56:42,243
mind if I create a little misunderstanding of my own?

865
00:56:42,703 --> 00:56:44,573
Create a misunderstanding?

866
00:56:45,073 --> 00:56:46,273
Because I saw something too.

867
00:56:51,743 --> 00:56:53,953
What kind of misunderstanding are you talking about?

868
00:57:13,573 --> 00:57:14,573
Mi Young.

869
00:57:15,373 --> 00:57:16,373
Yes?

870
00:57:16,643 --> 00:57:18,343
What's wrong? Is it not good?

871
00:57:19,543 --> 00:57:20,673
Oh, no.

872
00:57:22,613 --> 00:57:23,613
So what is going on?

873
00:57:24,143 --> 00:57:26,613
It is not like you to ask me to dinner.

874
00:57:41,933 --> 00:57:43,233
Why didn't you tell me?

875
00:57:44,163 --> 00:57:47,033
What didn't I tell you?

876
00:57:49,273 --> 00:57:50,973
The day you went to see your half-brothers.

877
00:57:52,573 --> 00:57:53,843
When you went to your family's home.

878
00:57:56,343 --> 00:57:57,413
You will be fine, right?

879
00:57:58,283 --> 00:58:00,383
If your brothers ask you questions, answer them well.

880
00:58:01,113 --> 00:58:03,583
And try to laugh at their jokes, even if they are not funny.

881
00:58:04,323 --> 00:58:06,723
You look angry when you are quiet.

882
00:58:07,223 --> 00:58:09,123
They do not care about things like that.

883
00:58:09,723 --> 00:58:11,023
They do not even like me that much.

884
00:58:11,223 --> 00:58:12,863
But they are still family.

885
00:58:13,533 --> 00:58:15,333
Deep down, your brothers might have been...

886
00:58:15,433 --> 00:58:16,903
hoping you would reach out first.

887
00:58:17,433 --> 00:58:19,073
If you approach them first,

888
00:58:19,233 --> 00:58:21,533
they will welcome you with open arms.

889
00:58:21,973 --> 00:58:24,543
Look at you, Mi Young. You are all grown up.

890
00:58:24,773 --> 00:58:25,873
Hey, I'm older than you.

891
00:58:32,883 --> 00:58:34,153
I will do my best.

892
00:58:36,423 --> 00:58:37,423
I love you.

893
00:58:38,153 --> 00:58:39,153
Me too.

894
00:58:39,623 --> 00:58:41,823
- Go get them. - Go get them.

895
00:58:43,863 --> 00:58:44,863
That day,

896
00:58:45,833 --> 00:58:48,093
something so terrible happened.

897
00:58:49,633 --> 00:58:50,803
Why didn't you tell me?

898
00:58:52,503 --> 00:58:55,403
Is that why you broke up with me?

899
00:58:57,973 --> 00:59:00,043
Because you were scared of your brothers' threats?

900
00:59:00,543 --> 00:59:01,543
Or...

901
00:59:02,683 --> 00:59:06,253
because you just could not give up management of the Calvin Hotel?

902
00:59:08,413 --> 00:59:09,923
I could give up everything else,

903
00:59:12,153 --> 00:59:13,893
but I could not give up that child.

904
00:59:16,993 --> 00:59:18,863
The child that woman was carrying at the time...

905
00:59:20,993 --> 00:59:22,033
I could not...

906
00:59:25,233 --> 00:59:26,733
let that child be born illegitimate like me.

907
00:59:28,433 --> 00:59:29,643
So that is why you got a divorce?

908
00:59:30,873 --> 00:59:31,873
Because that child...

909
00:59:34,613 --> 00:59:36,513
turned out not to be yours?

910
00:59:38,343 --> 00:59:39,353
Mi Young.

911
00:59:42,423 --> 00:59:43,423
All this time...

912
00:59:44,953 --> 00:59:47,293
All this time, I hated you so much.

913
01:00:41,543 --> 01:00:44,513
(Epilogue)

914
01:00:46,583 --> 01:00:47,583
Hey, Calvin.

915
01:01:09,673 --> 01:01:12,643
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

916
01:01:14,373 --> 01:01:16,683
- What is this? - I just changed my mind.

917
01:01:17,013 --> 01:01:20,113
This is what we call a classic backstab.

918
01:01:21,653 --> 01:01:24,323
- That psycho. - This operation's code name is...

919
01:01:24,383 --> 01:01:25,383
To that place.

920
01:01:26,523 --> 01:01:29,063
I have seen it all now.

921
01:01:29,563 --> 01:01:30,563
A drink...

922
01:01:30,623 --> 01:01:32,393
To think he would bring a woman into our home.

923
01:01:32,493 --> 01:01:33,893
I mean, is he out of his mind?

924
01:01:35,633 --> 01:01:37,863
If you're jealous, go ahead and bring someone over.

925
01:01:39,533 --> 01:01:41,203
You keep bringing up old wounds...

926
01:01:41,273 --> 01:01:42,503
and blaming other people. Please,

927
01:01:42,573 --> 01:01:43,903
just break that nasty habit of yours.

928
01:01:44,773 --> 01:01:46,273
Please, just shut up.

